# 10. Retry Strategy

Retry behavior should not be based only on whether an exception occurred.

Instead ask:

> If exactly the same request is executed again later, is there a reasonable possibility that it will succeed?

---

## 10.1 Generally Retryable

Typical retryable errors include:

```text
HTTP 429
HTTP 502
HTTP 503
HTTP 504
Connection reset
Temporary network failure
Upstream timeout
Database deadlock
Temporary service unavailable
```

---

## 10.2 Generally Not Retryable

Typical non-retryable errors include:

```text
Invalid parameter
Missing business parameter
Account not found
Permission denied
Business rule violation
Invalid authentication credentials
Programming error
Unexpected KeyError
Unexpected NoneType failure
```

---

## 10.3 Retryability Matrix

| Error | Retryable | Recommended Action |
|---|---:|---|
| Missing parameter | No | Correct parameter |
| Invalid account ID | No | Correct parameter |
| Account not found | No | Change parameter / ask user |
| Business rule violation | No | Inform user |
| HTTP 429 | Yes | Retry with backoff |
| HTTP 502 | Yes | Retry with backoff |
| HTTP 503 | Yes | Retry with backoff |
| HTTP 504 | Yes | Retry with backoff |
| Upstream timeout | Yes | Retry with backoff |
| DB deadlock | Usually | Retry |
| Permission denied | No | Correct authorization |
| Authentication failure | Usually no | Re-authenticate |
| Unexpected `KeyError` | No | Internal investigation |
| Unexpected programming exception | No | Internal investigation |

---

# 11. Retry Should Usually Occur Inside the Server First

Infrastructure retries should generally not be delegated immediately to the LLM.

Avoid:

```text
Tool
 ↓
Upstream timeout
 ↓
isError=true
 ↓
LLM
 ↓
Call Tool Again
```

Instead:

```text
Tool
 ↓
Upstream Call
 ↓
Timeout
 ↓
Server Retry #1
 ↓
Server Retry #2
 ↓
Still Failed
 ↓
Tool Error
 ↓
isError=true
 ↓
Model decides next action
```

This prevents unnecessary LLM orchestration for infrastructure-level transient failures.

Recommended retry strategy:

```text
bounded retry
+
exponential backoff
+
jitter
```

For example:

```python
MAX_RETRIES = 2
```

Do not implement unlimited retries.

---

# 12. Timeout Management

Every external dependency should have an explicit timeout.

Avoid:

```python
result = await call_upstream()
```

without a timeout policy.

Prefer:

```python
result = await asyncio.wait_for(
    call_upstream(),
    timeout=10,
)
```

or configure HTTP clients with explicit timeouts:

```python
Timeout(
    connect=2,
    read=8,
    write=5,
)
```

Without explicit timeouts:

```text
Upstream Service Hangs
        ↓
Tool Hangs
        ↓
MCP Request Hangs
        ↓
Client Eventually Times Out
```

At that point it becomes difficult to determine whether the failure originated from:

```text
Transport
MCP Server
Tool
Database
Upstream API
```

Therefore timeout boundaries should be explicitly defined.

---

# 13. Internal Errors Must Be Sanitized

Avoid:

```python
except Exception as exc:
    return str(exc)
```

This may expose internal information such as:

```text
Database hostnames
Internal URLs
SQL statements
Table names
Stack traces
File paths
AWS resources
Vendor endpoints
Customer identifiers
Token fragments
Implementation details
```

Instead separate:

```text
Server-side diagnostics
```

from:

```text
Client-visible error
```

Example:

```python
except Exception:
    error_id = str(uuid.uuid4())

    logger.exception(
        "Unexpected MCP tool error",
        extra={
            "error_id": error_id,
            "tool": "get_holdings"
        }
    )

    return tool_error(
        code="INTERNAL_ERROR",
        message="Unable to complete the request.",
        retryable=False,
        correlation_id=error_id,
    )
```

---

# 14. Logging Recommendation

Server logs should contain sufficient information for debugging.

Recommended fields:

```text
timestamp
correlation_id
request_id
tool_name
error_category
error_code
exception_type
upstream_service
retry_count
latency
stack_trace
```

Client responses should contain only safe information:

```text
error code
safe message
retryability
recommended action
correlation ID
```

Example:

```text
SERVER LOG
────────────────────────────────

error_id: 123456
tool: get_holdings
exception: KeyError
stack_trace: ...
upstream_service: account-api
request_id: xyz


CLIENT / MODEL
────────────────────────────────

code: INTERNAL_ERROR
message: Unable to complete request.
retryable: false
correlation_id: 123456
```

---

# 15. Recommended Error Handling Flow

A standardized MCP tool should conceptually follow this flow:

```text
Tool Request
      │
      ▼
Input Validation
      │
      ├── Invalid
      │      ↓
      │ ValidationError
      │
      ▼
Business Logic
      │
      ├── Business Failure
      │      ↓
      │ BusinessError
      │
      ▼
Dependency Layer
      │
      ├── Timeout
      │      ↓
      │ UpstreamTimeoutError
      │
      ├── HTTP 429
      │      ↓
      │ RateLimitError
      │
      └── HTTP 5xx
             ↓
        UpstreamError
             │
             ▼
         Error Mapper
             │
       ┌─────┴─────┐
       │           │
       ▼           ▼
 Expected       Unexpected
 Failure         Failure
       │           │
       ▼           ▼
 Tool Error    Internal Error
 isError=true       │
       │            ▼
       │       Server Logging
       │            +
       │       Sanitization
       │
       ▼
 Model Receives
 Actionable Error
```

---

# 16. Example Implementation Pattern

A tool may follow this pattern:

```python
@mcp.tool()
async def get_holdings(account_id: str):

    try:
        validate_account_id(account_id)

        return await holdings_service.get_holdings(
            account_id
        )

    except ValidationError as exc:

        return tool_error(
            code="INVALID_ACCOUNT_ID",
            category="validation",
            message=str(exc),
            retryable=False,
            action="correct_parameter",
        )

    except RateLimitError:

        return tool_error(
            code="UPSTREAM_RATE_LIMIT",
            category="upstream",
            message="The upstream service is temporarily rate limited.",
            retryable=True,
            action="retry",
        )

    except UpstreamTimeoutError:

        return tool_error(
            code="UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT",
            category="upstream",
            message="The holdings service timed out.",
            retryable=True,
            action="retry",
        )

    except UpstreamError:

        return tool_error(
            code="UPSTREAM_UNAVAILABLE",
            category="upstream",
            message="The holdings service is temporarily unavailable.",
            retryable=True,
            action="retry",
        )

    except Exception:

        correlation_id = generate_correlation_id()

        logger.exception(
            "Unexpected get_holdings failure",
            extra={
                "correlation_id": correlation_id
            }
        )

        return tool_error(
            code="INTERNAL_ERROR",
            category="internal",
            message="Unable to complete the request.",
            retryable=False,
            action="inform_user",
            correlation_id=correlation_id,
        )
```

